From 726488db9753ae7bec5e979213fc5097fd32b7bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 01:49:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix: incident-report code collisions silently dropping
 citizen reports
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

nextReportCode() generated codes from count()+1, so two concurrent
absorbs (background replay + a citizen report POST, or any parallel
ingests) read the same count, built the same RPT-XXXX code, and the
losing insert crashed with 'Unique constraint failed on the fields:
(code)' — the citizen's report never became an incident and no
notification was sent, while the API still returned 201.

- nextReportCode() now scans existing codes and uses max suffix + 1
  (count()+1 also re-issued used codes after any report deletion)
- report creation retries with a fresh code on P2002 instead of
  losing the report (bounded 8 attempts)
- pushNotification() treats a duplicate dedupe key as already-sent
  instead of failing the whole absorb (escalation race)
- ReportIncidentOverlay: fix react-hooks/set-state-in-effect
  violations (lazy initial loc state + async-only effect; step reset
  moved into submit()) and drop stale eslint-disable directives —
  lint is now 0 errors / 0 warnings
- add regression tests: concurrent code race, code reuse after
  deletion, citizen report E2E (all passing; full corpus replay at
  speed 600 creates 21 reports with unique sequential codes and
  zero absorb failures)
